      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-01-26_WidnesExaminer_art0032" n="art0032">
        <head>TO-DAY'S RECIPE.</head>
        <p>TO-DAY'S RECIPE.</p>
        <p>CELERY FRITTERS.-Trim, wash, and cut off the tops of as many roots of celery as you may :require, without dividing them, then boil for a .quarter of an hour. Remove them from the hot -water, and put. them in cold. Drain them and die two and two together. Cover the bottom of .a stewpan with slices of thini?•cut bacon, place in the celery, season with parsley, shallots, or green onions, a little salt, and moisten it with the fat taken off soup. Cover with slices of utwon ana a wen-buttered round at paper, waten them come to a boil, then let them simmer until done, drain and fry them in plenty- of butter. Drain, dish, and glaze them with castor sugar, by holding a red•hot poker over them, just be- fore sending 'them to table.</p>
      </div>
