      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-01-26_WidnesExaminer_art0037" n="art0037">
        <head>SCHOOLGIEL'S BLOUSE.</head>
        <p>SCHOOLGIEL'S BLOUSE.</p>
        <p>In our sketch we have depicted a neat every- day blouse for a schoolgirl. It could be carried out in either dark or light coloured delaine or flannel. If it is intended to be worn with a navy-blue costume then a dark-blue delaino, spotted with white, would be smart as well aa useful. The blouse ia fastened behind and the fulness arranged in tucks straight 'across the front and back to about yoke deep. Over the</p>
        <p>shoulders there are two straps of the material prettily adorned with a double row of feather- stitching in thick white silk. The straps are stitched to the blouse, the two shorter ones being left loose just in the centre, to allow the ends of the cravat to be passed beneath. The sleeves are of the useful bishop shape, and are drawn into rather long cuffs, which are finished at the wrist with a narrow feather-stitched strap.</p>
