      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-01-26_WidnesExaminer_art0038" n="art0038">
        <head>a/CAVE JACKETS.</head>
        <p>a/CAVE JACKETS.</p>
        <p>Short Zouave jackets of black velvet, embroi- dered liberally with sequins, form attractive ac- companiments to many of the tea-gowns of the day. They are regardless of any fitting, and are so made that they can easily be slipped over the gown, or may even be used over a silk or satin slip for home dinner wear. A dainty ex- ample of this description was made with tiny tight 'sleeves just covering the top of the arm, and edged all round with dagger-shaped bugles; the velvet being covered with an all-over design of jet embroidery and applications of flowers in black gauze outlined with chenille.</p>
        <p>cURED IN A NI.GFIT.</p>
