e MINOR POLICE CASES. former impersonations, and her undoubted accemplish- ' At the Occasional Court, on Saturday morning, before meats as an actress are not fully brought out. Mrs. Mr. S. Ormand, James Ince, collier of Earlestown, was Jennings makes a most motherly Mrs. Wake, while fined 2s 6d. and cost for being drunk and disorderly ; the smaller parts of Miss Wenham and Miss Rose and Catherine Carlin, of Eartesto.n 2s. 6d. for drunken- t‘v Williams, INalis3ionudraeyr, obr ;re Joseph -street, -lt Wallhead are both ably played. Quite one of the ."Ittrornhonlats. funniest interludes is the scene in Dr. Wake's waiting Helens, w'as fined 2s. 6d. and costs for having been room, ;Ind here Mrs. F. Griffiths makes an umnistake- drunk and disorderly. James Blioston, collier, Earles- able hit as the hen-pecking Mrs. Murdock. Miss town, also fined 2s. 61. and costs. P.C. Pickles proved Brundrett appears only in the first act, but as the the charges..ThomasNolan,of Earlestown, was charged forti -telling - • she is most realistic both in with _being drunk and disorderly (tried on Tuesday</p>
