      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-01-26_WidnesExaminer_art0110" n="art0110">
        <head>Warrington v Bradford.</head>
        <p>Warrington v Bradford.</p>
        <p>The return match between these clubs took place at Warrington on Saturday before 5,000 spectators. Neither side was at full strength, but an exciting and keenly-contested game took place. Owing to a slight frost and a sudden thaw the ground W#s very soft and holding though the weather conditions were favourable in the afternoon. Teams:— _</p>
        <p>Warrington—Berry, back ; Brooks, Tilley, Isher- wood, Hockenhall, three-quarter backs; Lees and Jenkins, halfbacks; Boardman,Thomas,Naylor, Shugars, Banner and Heath, forwards. Bradrord—Gunn, back; Decban, Connell, Cludetay, and Bedford, three-quarter backs ' - Surman and Brear, half-backs ; Greenwood, Smales, Mann, Feather, Walton, and Turner, forwards. Referee, Mr. W. %V. Taylor, Hunslet ; touch judges, Messrs. J. F. Brittain (Leigh) and W. Cawley (Runcorn.) The game opened directly in favour of Bradford, for after Gunn had defeated an attempt to invade by Lees and Jenkins, a brilliant dribbling moxement by the whole of the Bradford forwards, in which Greenwood and Smales were the leaders, forced the home custodian to save. Warrington got down to the Bradford end, and efforts to cross by Brooks and Isherwood were checked by Gunn. whcr eventually placed the visitors on the aggressive once more, and Connell making a mark in a good position, Surman placed Bradford two points to the good. By superior tack play War- rington got dangerous, but the Bradford forwards again exhibiting tine dribbling had the home line at their mercy until a rather hasty kick robbed them of a sub- stantial score. Near half-time Warrington pressed hard and after a fine round of passing, which Gunn and Declian checked on the line, Lees threw wide to Brooks, who was practically uncovered, and an easy try was the result. Thomas placed a goal. The Bradford forwards again became dangerous near the interval, but little support was forthcoming from behind, and when ends were changed Warrington led by five points to two points. Turning round, for a long time the game was of an even nature, the Bradford forwards more than counter- balancing the good work of the home backs. Brear and Surman made good runs, whilst Greenwood was held up by Berry after the greater part of the opposition bad been cleared. Warrington again became dangerous, and Brooks and Thomas were pulled up in turn. Cluderay had a kick charged, and Harmer scored. The last stages of the game were fought out in exciting fashion, for. brilliant work by the Bradford vanguard led the way to Dechan, whilst in the last minute Heath notched a try for Warrington. Reanit :—Warrington 1 goal 3 Pries (11 points), Bradford 1 goal 1 try (5 points).</p>
      </div>
