        <p>LANCASHIRE EDUCI EION COMM HIE 6. TO CONTRACTORS. The Lancashire Education Committee are prepared to receive TI3NDIIIIS FOR THB RI:MOTION of a BHW PUBLIC BLHNIHNTARY bCHOOL for 350 dcholars at Penketh, near Warrington. The Plans may be seen and Bills of Quantities obtained at the office of the County Architect. Mr. Henry littler. 16, Rithiesdale Place, Preston, by payment of a deposit of £2 (which will be returned upon receipt of a bona-fide tender) The Committee do not bind themselves to accept . the lowest or any tender. Tenders must be delivered before 12 o'clock noon on February 7th, 1907. sealed and endorsed, to G F. Clarke Esq.. Crow Lane West, Farleetown (Signed). HARCOURT E. CLARE. Clerk to the Lancashire County Council. County Offices. Preston, 1905. COUNTY BOROUO II OF W tai ttiGTON.— TO S (ORBS CON TRACTORS, HI.RTHENW AHH PIPH MANUFACTUURRi, QUARRY OWN/111S, MEM.. CHANTS, 'IIIAM OWSHRS. arc. The Paving and Sewerale Committee of the Council of the County Borough of Warrington is preptred to receive TIINDFIRS for the supply of the Committee's Requ'rense ts during the 12 mon' hs ending March 31,t, 1908 viz. : Granite of -yenita Cubes Concrete Fags Rawtenstall Kerbs Rawtenstall .etts Rawtenstall Flags Blue Bricks Chequered lies Sewer Pipes. Bends, Junctions, &amp;I. Cast Iron Gullies Macadam an I Chipping. Whitelime Chipping Sand Sea Gravel Copper Slag Spathe, Ptak., Masons' Tools, &amp;c. Brooms Street Sweeping M tohine Rotary Brooms Also for carting for the Highway and Scavenging Depart- ments for the 12 months. Parties wishing for tender forms will please specify th ose materials only forlwhich they propose to tender. Specifications, &amp;c., may be seen, and forms of t mier and all further information obtaineS at the office of the Borough Surveyor, Town Hail, on and after Toursday nest, the 31st instant, at which pise tenden, se tie I, mast be delivered on or before 12 o'clock noon on Saturday, 9th day of February, 1907. Any contractor whose te