        <p>STOCKTON HEATH. BAND OF HOPE CONCERT.—An entertainment was given in the Providence Schoolroom on Monday evening in connection with the Hill Cliffe and Stockton Heath United Band of Hope Society, at which there was a crowded attendance. Rev. J. S. Hughes, president of the society, presided. The principal attraction in the programme was the performance of the operettee "The Sleeping Beauty " by the members of Cairo-street Basd of Hop., which was exceedingly well given. Other itgine-were action song and drill" Gay little girls from Japan," by a number of girls who presented a very pretty spectacle. Miss Sophia Clatworthy delighted the audience with a well executed mandoline solo and was recalled, as was also Miss Rachael Peacock, for her excellent rendering of "The Gift." Considerable amusement was caused by the action song" Three modest Quakeresses," by the Misses E. and M. Mounfield and Emma Hamblett. The humorous element was in the bands of Mr. Bert Spruce, who provoked roars of laughter by his recitations. A hearty vote of thanks was given to the Cairo-street friends and all who had taken part in the entertainment on the proposition of Mr. G. Whitfield (secretary), seconded by Air. J. Pearse.</p>
